 a small waterfall just before the take out. More below.\n\nThis portion of the Roeliff Jansen Kill is mostly moving flat water with a number of good rapids towards the middle to later portion of the run, and a larger drop in the first half that may need a scout.\n\nThe main **Hazards** on this route is the abundant sweepers and strainers. A beaver dam will also require hauling over, or running at high water levels. Just before the take out there is a small waterfall. While experienced ww paddlers may wish to run it, levels permitting, open boaters will likely need to line or carry around it.\n\n**Catskills Area Reaches**\n\n[Basic Creek](content/River/view/river-detail/1242/) [Batavia Kill](content/River/view/river-detail/1243/) [Bear Kill](content/River/view/river-detail/1246/)\n\n[Beaver Kill (Delaware Trib)](content/River/view/river-detail/1247/) [Beaver Kill (Hudson Trib)](content/River/view/river-detail/1248/) [Beer Kill](content/River/view/river-detail/394/)\n\n[Beer Kill, W. Branch](content/River/view/river-detail/1250/) [Bowery Creek](content/River/view/river-detail/4101/) [Bush Kill](content/River/view/river-detail/1450/)\n\n[Callicoon Creek, E. Branch](content/River/view/river-detail/1267/) [Callicoon Creek, N. Branch](content/River/view/river-detail/1268/) [Catskill Creek (1.)](content/River/view/river-detail/1274/)\n\n[Catskill Creek (2.)](content/River/view/river-detail/1275/) [Catskill Creek (4.)](content/River/view/river-detail/1273/) [Claverack Creek](content/River/view/river-detail/10617/)\n\n[Coxing Kill](content/River/view/river-detail/4100/) [Delaware](content/River/view/river-detail/1291/) [Delaware, E. Branch](content/River/view/river-detail/1292/)\n\n[Delaware, W. Branch](content/River/view/river-detail/3416/) [Little Delaware](content/River/view/river-detail/3174/) [Dry Brook](content/River/view/river-detail/1293/)\n\n[East Kill](content/River/view/river-detail/1296/) [Esopus Creek (1)](content/River/view/river-detail/3849/) [Esopus Creek (2